    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW24q3T9CwWwRn94Pkb1THGGV)_\n\n## Summary\nNew module `sp-litnotes-titles` (section of `docs/tangles/academic/sp-academic.org`, required by `sp-litnotes`). Litnotes are identified by `ROAM_REFS` now, so the title no longer has to be the citekey.\n\n- `M-x sp-litnotes-titles-report` is a dry run (writes nothing): per note, the references, old and new `#+title:` (from `pub-title`), old and new file name, and `file:` links elsewhere that name the old file. Skipped or flagged: no `:ID:` drawer, no or empty `pub-title`, a file name in neither scheme, a title with no slug, a new name that already exists or that two notes would share, case-only changes; notes that share a title are listed too.\n- `M-x sp-litnotes-titles-apply` shows that report, asks once, copies each note to `var/litnote-title-backups/<time>/`, writes the title, renames the file, then `vulpea-db--forget-file` (old path), `org-id-add-location` and `vulpea-db-update-file` (same calls as `sp-split--denote-rename`). The `:ID:` is checked unchanged after the write; locked files and files with unsaved buffers are skipped.\n- File names: Denote `ID--slug__keywords.org` (the litnotes of citar-denote) and `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_slug.org` are read; the identifier, separator and keywords stay and only the slug is rebuilt (lower case, ASCII, 100 characters at most; `sp-litnotes-titles-slug-function`). `sp-litnotes-titles-rename-files` nil copies titles only.\n- Independent of the `ROAM_REFS` conversion of #210: it can run before or after it.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] 6 ERT tests (`tests/sp-litnotes-titles-test.el`) in Emacs 29.3 batch with a temporary vault: statuses, slugs and names, report writes nothing, apply writes and is idempotent, unsaved buffer skipped. Tangle check passes.\n- [ ] Run `M-x sp-litnotes-titles-report` on the real `~/notes/litnotes` and read it before `sp-litnotes-titles-apply` (commit or back up the notes first).\n- [ ] Not run: the real Vulpea database calls, a real vault.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiB6VndotVEWsSCDXPL)_",
